  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Text attributes
  </title>
  <p>
    Text attributes describe the font, style, alignment, colors, and other formatting associated
    with text. The information available to Orca depends on which attributes the application
    exposes to assistive technologies.
  </p>
  <section id="checking-formatting">
    <title>Checking formatting</title>
    <p>
      The settings and commands below let you choose which formatting information Orca presents
      and inspect the attributes of the current character.
    </p>
    <section id="settings-checking-formatting">
      <title>Settings</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Text Attributes</gui> category.
      </p>
      <p>
        The list contains one row for each text attribute. Use the presentation mode on a row to
        choose whether Orca speaks the attribute, marks it in braille, does both, or does
        neither. Use the row menu or drag handle to change the order in which attributes are
        presented. The speech choices apply when you request the current character's formatting;
        they do not filter automatic formatting-change announcements.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Text Attributes</gui>: Lists text
            attributes and lets you choose whether each is spoken, marked in braille, both, or
            neither. The choices and presentation order can be customized for individual
            applications. Speech choices apply to the explicit formatting command, not automatic
            formatting-change announcements. Enable braille marking for the mistake attribute to
            mark spelling and grammar errors. Choices: None, Speak, Mark in braille, Speak and
            mark.
          </p>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>None</gui>: Does not present the
                attribute.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Speak</gui>: Speaks the attribute.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Mark in braille</gui>: Marks the
                attribute in braille.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Speak and mark</gui>: Speaks the
                attribute and marks it in braille.
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Reorder</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute earlier or later in the presentation order.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move to top</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute to the top of the list.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move up one</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute up one position.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move down one</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute down one position.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Move to bottom</gui>: Moves the selected
                text attribute to the bottom of the list.
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
    <section id="commands-checking-formatting">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Object details</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Present character formatting</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>F</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
          <p>
            Presents the configured attributes for the current character, omitting attributes
            whose values are treated as defaults. Uses the character at the flat review location
            when flat review is active, or at the text caret otherwise. If no formatting
            information is available, Orca tells you.
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Show character formatting</gui>: <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>F</key>
            </keyseq>
            (press twice quickly)
          </p>
          <p>
            Opens a window showing all available attributes for the current character, including
            those not enabled for speech. You can inspect and copy the details. Press <key>Escape</key> to close the window. Uses
            the character at the flat review location when flat review is active, or at the text
            caret otherwise. If no formatting information is available, Orca tells you.
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
  <section id="automatic-announcements">
    <title>Automatic announcements</title>
    <p>
      Orca can announce formatting changes, such as bold or italic, as you move through text.
      The settings below control these announcements. Applications can also expose spelling and
      grammar errors as text attributes, often corresponding to a squiggly underline on screen.
      Configure those announcements in "<link xref="features_speech_and_voices_verbosity#settings-verbosity">Verbosity preferences</link>".
    </p>
    <section id="settings-automatic-announcements">
      <title>Settings</title>
      <section id="settings-automatic-announcements-speech-presenter-verbosity">
        <title>Verbosity</title>
        <p>
          <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
          <gui>Speech</gui> category, <gui>Verbosity</gui> group.
        </p>
        <p>
          <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Text attribute changes</gui>: Controls automatic
              announcements of formatting changes as you navigate. These announcements are
              independent of the attribute list used by the explicit formatting command.
              Choices: Off (default), Editable text only, Always.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </section>
      <section id="settings-automatic-announcements-say-all-presenter-say-all">
        <title>Say All</title>
        <p>
          <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
          <gui>Say All</gui> category.
        </p>
        <p>
          <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Text attribute changes</gui>: Controls automatic
              announcements of formatting changes during Say All, independently of announcements
              during navigation and the attribute list used by the explicit formatting command.
              Choices: Off, Editable text only, Always.
            </p>
            <list>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Off (default)</gui>: Does not announce
                  formatting changes.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Editable text only</gui>: Announces
                  formatting changes only in editable text.
                </p>
              </item>
              <item>
                <p>
                  <gui>Always</gui>: Always announces
                  formatting changes.
                </p>
              </item>
            </list>
          </item>
        </list>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section id="commands-automatic-announcements">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Speech and verbosity</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Cycle to the next text attribute change mode</gui>: Unbound by
            default.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cycles through formatting-change announcement modes for the current session.
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
  <section id="braille-indicators">
    <title>Braille indicators</title>
    <p>
      Braille indicators mark formatting without adding words to the display. They are
      independent of spoken formatting announcements. Configure the indicator in "<link xref="features_braille_display_settings">Display settings</link>".
    </p>
  </section>
</page>
